    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 7th with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who secures our top efficiency score of 82.13. His matchup against Lowder (4.77 xERA) is the most favorable of the slate, bolstered by a significant platoon advantage and a wind-aided environment that enhances his power-speed profile. While **Junior Caminero** occupies a strong spot at 71.24, his value is derived from his premium position in the order (#3) against a favorable lefty in Bennett. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** remains a mandatory start at 66.01; despite facing a modest xERA in Ginn, the combination of his leadoff positioning and the elevated stolen base potential against a battery with a slow delivery keeps his floor well within elite territory. **Kyle Schwarber** rounds out the lineup at 61.85, relying on a strong xwOBA and the leadoff-adjacent protection of the #2 hole to offset a neutral matchup.\n\nOur decision-making process was heavily influenced by the scarcity of stolen bases in this 5x5 format, which is why **Caleb Durbin** holds a roster spot despite a marginal 42.95 rating. His batting order placement (#9) is a significant drag on his score, yet his elite speed against an opponent with a slow delivery provides an isolated, category-specific utility that overrides his poor lineup positioning. We are currently navigating the absences of **Yordan Alvarez**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** due to scheduling, alongside the long-term caution required for the sidelined **Christian Yelich**. With depth options like **Colt Keith**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** waiting in the wings, we continue to monitor the daily volatility of our bench. Today, no bench player eclipsed the starters' efficiency, allowing us to preserve our game caps while awaiting healthier matchups for the remainder of the rotation.",
